  "blueprint_md": "# Automation blueprint: Zoning design and quote for installers\n\n## Process summary\n\n- **Description:** Installers send the floor plans of a home or office and ask a manufacturer of zoned HVAC controls for a zoning design and a quote. A pre-sales engineer reads the plans, sizes the zones and builds the bill of materials.\n- **Owner:** Pre-sales Engineering\n- **Executions per month:** 240\n- **Steps:** 6\n- **Analysis:** <timestamp>, process version 1, rules scoring-v1, LLM ok (fake/fake-deterministic-v1)\n\n## Current state\n\n- **Monthly hours:** 308.00\n- **Monthly cost:** 9,856.00\n\n## Automation opportunities\n\nOrdered by monthly time. Suitability measures whether a step can be automated, not how much it is worth.\n\n| # | Step | Method | Human control | Decided by | Hours/month | Suitability |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---:|---:|\n| 3 | Size the zones, dampers and grilles | HYBRID | REQUIRED | AI | 120.00 | 40 |\n| 2 | Take rooms, areas and the existing unit from the plans | AI_CANDIDATE | NONE | RULES | 100.00 | 53 |\n| 4 | Build the bill of materials and the quote | RULE_BASED | NONE | RULES | 40.00 | 100 |\n| 6 | Send the quote and follow up | HYBRID | NONE | AI | 24.00 | 55 |\n| 5 | Technical review of large projects | HYBRID | REQUIRED | AI | 12.00 | 28 |\n\n- **Size the zones, dampers and grilles:** Input is digital structured and integration readiness is partial.\n- **Take rooms, areas and the existing unit from the plans:** unstructured digital input without required human judgement\n- **Build the bill of materials and the quote:** clear rules over structured digital input with few exceptions\n- **Send the quote and follow up:** Input is mixed and integration readiness is unknown.\n- **Technical review of large projects:** Input is digital structured and integration readiness is none.\n\n## Proposed architecture\n\n- Workflow engine that runs the steps in order, with retries and an audit log\n- Rules step in the workflow engine with explicit, versioned validation rules\n- Model-based extraction or classification behind a schema-validated contract\n- Automated draft with a person confirming the result\n- Human review queue: flagged items wait for a decision, which is logged\n- Orchestrate the automated steps from a single workflow engine with retries\n- Route low-confidence and flagged items to a human review queue\n\n## Business impact\n\nEvery economic figure below depends on the assumptions listed after it.\n\n- **Hours freed per month:** 142.00\n- **Gross monthly savings:** 4,544.00\n- **Monthly tooling cost:** 50.00\n- **Net monthly savings:** 4,494.00\n- **Implementation cost:** 6,000.00\n- **Payback (months):** 1.34\n- **ROI at 12 months:** 799 %\n\n**Assumptions**\n\n- Implementation cost: 6,000.00\n- Monthly tooling cost: 50.00\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-1>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-2>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-3>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-4>: 50 %\n- Expected time reduction for step <step-5>: 50 %\n- 1 step(s) have no expected reduction and count as zero savings\n\n## Risks\n\n- [RULES / DATA] Receive the request and the floor plans handles sensitive data\n- [AI / STEP] Data protection: restrict access and log processing\n- [RULES / OPERATIONAL] Size the zones, dampers and grilles depends on human judgement\n- [RULES / OPERATIONAL] Technical review of large projects is business critical\n- [AI / OPERATIONAL] Exceptions need an owner once the happy path is automated\n\n## Human controls\n\n- **Receive the request and the floor plans:** REQUIRED. handles sensitive data; Reviewer decision: Reviewer keeps this step manual\n- **Size the zones, dampers and grilles:** REQUIRED. requires human judgement\n- **Technical review of large projects:** REQUIRED. requires human approval\n\n## Workflow specification\n\n1. Trigger: a new process execution starts\n2. Receive the request and the floor plans: MANUAL, then wait for a person to approve before continuing\n3. Take rooms, areas and the existing unit from the plans: AI_CANDIDATE\n4. Size the zones, dampers and grilles: HYBRID, then wait for a person to approve before continuing\n5. Build the bill of materials and the quote: RULE_BASED\n6. Technical review of large projects: HYBRID, then wait for a person to approve before continuing\n7. Send the quote and follow up: HYBRID\n8. End: record the outcome and the time spent for later comparison\n",
